<h2 id="filters">Filter and sort the table</h2>
<p class="sub">The table below has 155 rows, every one a card at least 2 of the 71 real Mardu-color Standard decks actually run. <b>72</b> still cost you wildcards. <b>common/uncommon</b> cards are left out: you hold 874 uncommon and 1016 common wildcards, so they never gate a build. <strong>Hide lands</strong> shows only spells. <strong>Hide already at 4-of</strong> shows only cards you still need (a "playset" is 4 copies because that's the deck-building limit). <strong>Hide rotating in early 2027</strong> drops the cards that leave Standard at the next rotation, which lands with the first release of 2027 and retires seven sets: Wilds of Eldraine (WOE), The Lost Caverns of Ixalan (LCI), Murders at Karlov Manor (MKM), Outlaws of Thunder Junction (OTJ), The Big Score (BIG), Bloomburrow (BLB) and Duskmourn: House of Horror (DSK). The filter reads every printing of each card rather than the one set shown in its row, because a card reprinted into a surviving set keeps its place in Standard. All three filters start ON; click a lit button to turn it off. For sorting, use the <strong>Wildcards needed</strong> and <strong>Deck count</strong> buttons, or click any column header. (Win rate is a per-deck number, not a per-card one, so its sort lives down in the 25-deck section below.)</p>
